y relationships. <span><span class="ref-journal">Carbohydr Polym. </span>1995;<span class="ref-vol">28</span>:3–14.</span></div></div><div class="ref-cit-blk" id="B5"><div class="ref-label">5.</div><div class="ref-cit">Browder, W; Williams, D; Lucore, P; Pretus, H; Jones, E; McNamee, R. Effect of enhanced macrophage function on early wound healing. <span><span class="ref-journal">Surgery. </span>1988;<span class="ref-vol">104</span>:224–230.</span>  <span style="white-space: nowrap;">[<a class="ref-extlink" href="redirect3.cgi?&amp;&amp;auth=0bIAZbOjUCY-e1L8kFOwo8sQ2ZFBNiJ9XqJZJ9AML&amp;reftype=pubmed&amp;artid=98428&amp;article-id=98428&amp;iid=2653&amp;issue-id=2653&amp;jid=87&amp;journal-id=87&amp;FROM=Article%7CCitationRef&amp;TO=Entrez%7CPubMed%7CRecord&amp;rendering-type=normal&amp;&amp;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/3261048">PubMed</a>]</span></div></div><div class="ref-cit-blk" id="B6"><div class="ref-label">6.</div><div class="ref-cit">Compton, R; Williams, D; Browder, W. The beneficial effect of enhanced macrophage function on the healing of bowel anastomoses. <span><span class="ref-journal">Am Surg. </span>1996;<span class="ref-vol">62</span>:14–18.</span>  <span style="white-space: nowrap;">[<a class="ref-extlink" href="redirect3.cgi?&amp;&amp;auth=0rGchrAGMG028fu63FrC3i5snet-JDW52Q4dFT5Mx&amp;reftype=pubmed&amp;artid=98428&amp;article-id=98428&amp;iid=2653&amp;issue-id=2653&amp;jid=87&amp;journal-id=87&amp;FROM=Article%7CCitationRef&amp;TO=Entrez%7CPubMed%7CRecord&amp;rendering-type=normal&amp;&amp;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/8540639">PubMed</a>]</span></div></div><div class="ref-cit-blk" id="B7"><div class="ref-label">7.</div><div class="ref-cit">Di Renzo, L; Yefenof, E; Klein, E. The function of human NK cells is enhanced by &#x003b2;-glucan, a ligand of CR3 (CD11b/CD18). <span><span class="ref-journal">Eur J Immunol. </span>1991;<span class="ref-vol">21</span>:1755–1758.</span>  <span style="white-space: nowrap;">[<a class="ref-extlink" hr